    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d677">

                <pb facs="0967" n="957" xml:id="pg957"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2–2546: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in China </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-03-05T19:00:00-05:00">March 5, 1946—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>403. For General Marshall. Colonel Webber will be made available (Your 359, Feb
                    25) and is now studying background of previous negotiations. He will leave at
                    earliest possible date, perhaps within a week. Colonel Pforzheimer will not be
                    available in the immediate future as he is now in ETO<anchor n="88"
                        xml:id="d677-f1"/> and will probably be recalled to Washington soon for
                    important negotiations here. However, if after matter has been fully discussed
                    with Colonel Webber it is still considered that BOWD<anchor n="89"
                        xml:id="d677-f2"/> representative is necessary, Colonel Pforzheimer’s
                    availability can be re-examined.</p>
                <p>It is recommended that scope of talks with Chinese as suggested by T. V. Soong
                    not be defined until after discussion with Colonel Webber. However it is
                    understood that these preliminary talks will not include any discussion of the
                    dollar valuation of yuan obligations. State, Treasury and War agree that Adler
                    should participate in talks.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
